the high-level motivation, which is that we view  

38
00:03:32,639 --> 00:03:39,919
solving this interconnect bottleneck as one of the 
core major hardware-level bottlenecks that needs  

39
00:03:39,919 --> 00:03:45,679
to be solved to keep the AI roadmaps running. 
Now if we double-click into that a little bit,  

40
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:51,920
the bottlenecks are coming from these electrical 
interconnects that exist in the so-called scale-up  

41
00:03:51,919 --> 00:03:58,799
fabric. The scale-up fabric connects a number 
of GPUs and AI accelerators together. You've got  

42
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:06,959
this issue in electrical interconnects where the 
faster you want to go—the more data you want to  

43
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:12,560
send between these GPUs and accelerators—the 
shorter distance you can go. We call that the  

44
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:20,639
bandwidth-distance trade-off. The only way we 
know how to solve this from first principles,  

45
00:04:21,199 --> 00:04:28,479
from the ground up, is to swap over to optical 
connectivity. That's where we say we've got to get  

46
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:36,240
a new generation of deeply integrated, CMOS-scale 
optical connectivity into the scale-up fabric,  

47
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:43,360
solve this bottleneck from the ground up where 
the real physics problem is happening, and then  

48
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:51,680
we enter the promised land beyond. So that's the 
quick snapshot of what Ayar Labs is trying to do.

49
