technologies are close enough to solve my problem,  

172
00:19:55,839 --> 00:20:01,279
and what supply chains are supporting and 
delivering them. You can have the greatest  

173
00:20:01,279 --> 00:20:06,879
technology in the world, but if you can't 
ramp true volume production, it's not a  

174
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:15,040
solution for customers trying to build high-volume 
rack-scale architectures and deploy them on time.  

175
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:21,519
Everyone's optimizing for their time to 
the first token that generates revenue.

176
00:20:21,519 --> 00:20:23,898
Ben (19:45.711)
Mm.

177
00:20:23,898 --> 00:20:25,039
Mark Wade (20:01.896)
So yeah, I think in the  

178
00:20:25,039 --> 00:20:34,960
short term we're going to live through a chaotic, 
turbulent set of technologies and form factors.  

179
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:43,840
But in the longer term, we're going to land 
this new generation of silicon photonics into a  

180
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:53,520
TSMC-like foundry plus OSAT flow. Companies 
